---
layout: changelog
title: "Disposable email detection now covers nearly 100K domains"
date: 2026-10-28
tags: auth, security
---

We added about 26,000 new throwaway email domains to Appwrite's disposable email detection, bringing the total to nearly 100,000 blocked domains.

Disposable addresses are a common way to abuse free resources, create fraudulent accounts, and support other malicious activity. With the [**Deny disposable emails**](/docs/products/auth/email-policies#deny-disposable-emails) policy enabled, sign-ups and email updates from these providers are rejected before an account is created.

Projects that already have the policy enabled are protected by the expanded list automatically. To turn it on, open **Auth** > **Policies** in the Appwrite Console, or call `updateDenyDisposableEmailPolicy` from any server SDK.

We will keep updating the list as new disposable email services appear.

